WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.800
This is not the Russian flag, but the flag of Slovakia, and this is also not the Russian flag, but the flag of Slovenia.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:12.740
And now you get it, I could mess with you a third time and say: and this is Russia, then flip it upside down and say it is Serbia.

3
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.000
But I am not that kind of person.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.260
Recently we got to see that Australians do not really tell the Serbian and Russian flags apart very well.

5
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.350
And I will be honest with you, I cannot judge them that much either.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.910
Come on, do you really tell the flag of Australia from the flag of New Zealand?

7
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.480
Well, you do, because you are an educated person.

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:38.000
But both have a blue background and the British Union Jack, because they are ex-British colonies, and they differ in the number and colors of the stars.

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.270
And I am aware that I presented it as if it were a big difference, but really it is not.

10
00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.520
They even have the same meaning.

11
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:49.350
The Australian flag has this big white star with seven points, which represents the Australian commonwealth.

12
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.280
A community, get it?

13
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:56.400
Six points represent the six Australian states, while the seventh represents all the Australian territories.

14
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:04.720
Although conspiracy theorists like to say it is dedicated to New Zealand, because the great Australian hegemonists have not gotten over the fact that it is not under Canberra's control.

15
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:14.340
Here you also have these four smaller stars, also with seven points, clear symbolism, but then you also have this fifth, smaller star with five points, because it supposedly shines weaker, never mind.

16
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.030
These stars together form the constellation Southern Cross.

17
00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.110
Why is that constellation so important to them?

18
00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:27.240
Well, because it is the brightest thing you can see in the sky of the southern hemisphere, and long ago sailors used it as a replacement for GPS.

19
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:34.960
And New Zealand has four red stars with five points each, outlined with white, which together represent the same thing.

20
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.920
Fine, but why are they so similar?

21
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.420
Because they are British colonies.

22
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:41.880
Fine, but why did they not change it now that both are independent?

23
00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:48.330
Because they cannot agree on who should change it, because they cannot agree on who came up with it first.

24
00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:54.320
Some New Zealanders think that Australia stole their flag and that they should then come up with something new.

25
00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.620
And I mean, New Zealand did adopt its flag first, in 1902.

26
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:04.320
But Australia held a competition for its flag design a year earlier and got this.

27
00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.920
It just started using it only in 1954.

28
00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:11.800
And because of that you can argue that Australia came up with this flag first.

29
00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:17.530
And just to put whipped cream on this cake of complications: the winning flag was designed by a New Zealander.

30
00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.040
I mean, look, it is irrelevant anyway who was first.

31
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:27.920
Because both flags came about by simply copy-pasting what all the other British colonies were already doing: the Union Jack and a blue background.

32
00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.620
And you are not even aware to what extent they practiced that.

33
00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:40.150
Australia can change its flag to one of the proposed versions, while New Zealand held a referendum where people chose five out of over ten thousand proposed designs.

34
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:43.080
In the end they were all meh, so that fell through.

35
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.590
It is hard to change a design.

36
00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:52.530
And then you have to print millions of new flags to replace the old ones, and not only in your country but everywhere in the world where they fly.

37
00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.060
So, in short: white stars Australia, red ones New Zealand.

38
00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.280
There is nothing to miss.

39
00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.250
Well, those are two similar flags.

40
00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.760
However, the problem arises when you have three very similar flags.

41
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.300
Specifically those of Colombia, Venezuela and Ecuador.

42
00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:15.920
These three countries were once part of Gran Colombia, which admittedly also included Panama and some parts of the surrounding countries, but all of them went their own way with their flags, so never mind.

43
00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:26.490
All of this once belonged to Spain, but as nationalism came to life in the 19th century, not only in Europe but around the world, the colonized territories began to demand independence.

44
00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:30.450
And one of the people who dreamed of it was Francisco de Miranda.

45
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:39.120
His modest vision was to unite the whole of Latin America, which was more on the level of my EU4 ambitions, so his wish did not come true.

46
00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.280
At least not to that extent.

47
00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:45.090
After his death some mini version of that idea arises in the form of Gran Colombia.

48
00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:50.000
The new state was named after Christopher Columbus, as de Miranda had imagined.

49
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.080
But he also imagined the flag of the new state, a yellow-blue-red tricolor.

50
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.860
And that after a conversation with none other than Goethe, small world.

51
00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:07.940
Yellow represents nobility and light, blue is a mixture of excitement and tranquility, while red is the exaltation of yellow and blue, a synthesis, the vanishing of light into shadow.

52
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.500
Yes, it sounds pretentious, but that is philosophy for you.

53
00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:18.090
For us ordinary mortals, the symbolism of these colors can be: the gold of Venezuela, which the ocean separates from bloody Spain.

54
00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.180
Fine, that is already a somewhat more brutal interpretation.

55
00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.040
Be that as it may, the lifespan of Gran Colombia was short.

56
00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:31.320
Still, after its breakup, apart from Panama, these three kept the same tricolor, because they do share a common history.

57
00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:37.870
Venezuela added eight stars to its flag, of which seven represent the seven original provinces of this country.

58
00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:43.540
I say original, because the eighth represents part of another country, Guyana, part of which once belonged to Venezuela.

59
00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:56.040
Of course, Guyana is not exactly a big fan of this flag, but the former Venezuelan president Hugo Chávez justified it by saying that the famous Simón Bolívar imagined the flag this way after he liberated that territory and annexed it to Venezuela.

60
00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:04.210
Ecuador changed the order of the stripes and added a shield with the mountain Chimborazo, from which the river Guayas originates, all natural resources of this country.

61
00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:10.420
At the top you have the sun and the signs of the zodiac, which represent the months of their revolution, so as not to drag out the story.

62
00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:16.340
The condor at the top represents the power of Ecuador, and around it you have four flags that represent four flags.

63
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:22.850
This on the left is the laurel that represents the victory of the republic, this on the right a palm leaf as a symbol of martyrs in the struggle for freedom.

64
00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:27.820
And at the bottom you have the fasces, which the Romans originally used to show the strength of unity.

65
00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:31.500
Because, like, you will easily break one rod, but you will have a harder time breaking a bundle.

66
00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:36.560
Of course, this became a bit of an awkward symbol in the 20th century, because Mussolini used it too.

67
00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.720
Because of that it is also associated with fascist movements, plus fasces is the root of the word fascism.

68
00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.990
Still, Ecuador has used it since the 1900s.

69
00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:48.020
Look, I would like one of my videos to be relevant for once, so let us move on.

70
00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.020
Oh yes, and Colombia changed only the order of the stripes.

71
00:05:51.020 --> 00:06:00.150
Anyway, the idea of several countries using the same colors to symbolize a common struggle for independence is, as you can guess, very popular in Africa.

72
00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:05.980
And there you have two types of flags, green-yellow-red and red-black-green, both very common on the continent.

73
00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:14.070
The first combination was inspired by Ethiopia, which in 1896 successfully repelled Italian attempts at colonization and thereby confirmed its independence.

74
00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:19.470
Of course, as the country changed its forms of government, it also changed the emblems on its flags.

75
00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:22.020
But still, this combination stayed forever.

76
00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.260
Green represents wealth and fertile land, as well as hope.

77
00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:30.430
Yellow also represents hope, while red, you probably know very well by now what it represents.

78
00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:34.800
This star with rays on the blue background represents the country's bright future.

79
00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:44.620
Ethiopia's success in repelling the colonizers and thus remaining the only country in Africa that Europeans never colonized, apart from Liberia, inspired the president of Ghana so much.

80
00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:50.190
And when they fought for independence from the United Kingdom, they used the three colors of Ethiopia.

81
00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:56.040
They just rearranged them, and later a black star was added, which symbolizes the emancipation of African peoples.

82
00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:07.960
The same trend was soon followed by Guinea, and then Mali, Cameroon, Senegal, Togo, Comoros, Burkina Faso, Seychelles, Guinea-Bissau, São Tomé and Príncipe, Congo, Mozambique, Zimbabwe, Mauritania and Benin.

83
00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.260
It is possible that some of these do not belong, possible that some others do.

84
00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:14.380
Hard to say because there is no precise definition everywhere.

85
00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:22.020
These colors no longer represented only an individual struggle against colonialism, but the continent's common struggle for the emancipation of Africans.

86
00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:30.810
Because of that, upon gaining independence, many of these states also tried to join various federations, but due to various problems they never succeeded.

87
00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:35.960
In any case, what remained common to them in that struggle are precisely these pan-African flag colors.

88
00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.000
You can even consider the flag of Chad pan-African, but we will get to that.

89
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:46.640
This second pan-African color combination, red-black-green, has a very close meaning to the first pan-African flag.

90
00:07:46.640 --> 00:08:08.940
The community that advocated for the rights of all Africans around the world defined these three colors as pan-African, where red represented blood shed for freedom, black the community of peoples, but again not at the level of states but at the level of the whole continent, which shows the desire for a united, strong Africa in the fight against colonialism, while green represented the natural wealth of Africa.

91
00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:17.050
This combination is used by Kenya, South Sudan and Malawi, but, quite likely, also by Saint Kitts and Nevis, and that in the Caribbean.

92
00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:17.540
How come?

93
00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:21.560
Because of the struggle of people who were forcibly taken from Africa there into slavery.

94
00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:32.360
The South African flag is a mixture of the flag of their anti-apartheid party with almost pan-African colors and the old flag, which is a mix of the Dutch and the British one, because they colonized them.

95
00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:37.580
Still, Africans are not the only ones who applied common symbolism on their flags.

96
00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.800
The Slavic states did the same.

97
00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:52.700
The flags of Slovakia, Slovenia, Serbia, Croatia, Czechia, Russia, but also of the Sorbs, of Republika Srpska within Bosnia and Herzegovina, of former Yugoslavia and until relatively recently Montenegro, all used pan-Slavic colors.

98
00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:56.900
That does not necessarily mean that all these peoples started using these colors because of it.

99
00:08:56.900 --> 00:09:02.280
They are called pan-Slavic colors precisely because they have always often been present among Slavic peoples.

100
00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:06.070
Okay, all that is nice, Igor, but what on earth are pan-Slavic colors?

101
00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:08.510
We actually talked about that five years ago.

102
00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:09.560
Half a decade, hey.

103
00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:17.500
Pan-Slavism is a political movement whose goal was the liberation, and then the unification, of all Slavic peoples into one large state.

104
00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:21.640
Ideal examples of that movement were Czechoslovakia and of course Yugoslavia.

105
00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.200
Okay, maybe not quite ideal examples because they failed, but you get it.

106
00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:35.300
Inspired by national revolutions across Europe, in 1848 the first pan-Slavic congress was organized in Prague, where representatives of all Slavic peoples gathered.

107
00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:43.580
And right there and then this pan-Slavic flag was proposed, quite possibly modeled on the Russian flag as the strongest Slavic state.

108
00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:49.980
And yes, it was precisely the pan-Slavic flag that served as inspiration for the flag of Yugoslavia, all versions of Yugoslavia.

109
00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:55.100
Still, as I said, not all Slavs started using these colors because of the pan-Slavic congress.

110
00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.920
On the contrary, let us look at ourselves first.

111
00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:09.150
The Serbs used these colors as early as the 13th century, in the Nemanjić era, since back then only rulers and nobles used coats of arms and flags, and during the uprising they used flags that contained all three colors.

112
00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:15.080
Then, under the Sretenje Constitution of 1835, we arrived at this flag, so 13 years before the congress in Prague.

113
00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:21.100
There is even a story that during Karađorđe's rule a delegation of Serbs went to Russia to ask for help in the uprising.

114
00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:26.110
However, when they got there, some parade was being held, for which flags were logically needed.

115
00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:32.760
And since of course they had none, but did not want to miss a good time, they decided to just take the Russian flag and turn it upside down.

116
00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:39.620
It seems that everyone present had the intellectual abilities of the average resident of southern Banat, because in the end nobody figured it out.

117
00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.750
Of course, this story is just a myth, because it is terribly banal.

118
00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:48.420
But it is considered that this kind of Serbian flag was inspired by the French one, because I am not sure what is unclear to you.

119
00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:56.210
Of course, because of the reminder of revolutionary France, this flag, and the constitution in general, bothered the empires, so it had to be changed.

120
00:10:56.210 --> 00:11:02.280
And that into this Russian-ish flag with just four stars added in the corner to show loyalty to the sultan.

121
00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:07.620
So the flags of these two powers in combination with historical colors inspired this kind of tricolor.

122
00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:12.410
I made a detailed video about this five years ago, but the quality is not really representative.

123
00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:17.280
So if you are interested in a quality remake, leave a like and I will do this topic better.

124
00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:22.660
And since we are on the subject of Russians, their tricolor actually came about modeled on the Dutch tricolor.

125
00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:27.930
The Dutch were excellent seafarers, and a need arose to mark their ships with flags.

126
00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:38.040
Well, the Russian tsar Peter the Great was a big fanboy of European seafaring, so he traveled to Amsterdam, among other things to pick up new shipbuilding skills from the hosts.

127
00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:43.420
And they impressed him so much there that he got inspiration for his empire's flag from them.

128
00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:49.330
This flag was originally used only on merchant ships, and very quickly became popular internationally.

129
00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:52.540
In time it would inspire the flag of the pan-Slavic movement.

130
00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:53.090
Probably.

131
00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:55.580
I am telling you, everyone else was already using these colors.

132
00:11:55.700 --> 00:12:03.520
But it is very likely that because of that movement some template came about and that as a sign of solidarity everyone started using horizontal tricolors of these colors.

133
00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:09.950
By the way, the Dutch flag very likely inspired the French tricolor as well, as a symbol of the transition from monarchy to republic.

134
00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:12.840
Except that the Netherlands is now a monarchy again, but never mind.

135
00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:23.060
So, if we consider that pan-Slavic flags were inspired by the Russian and French ones, and the Russian and French by the Dutch one, it means the Dutch are the creators of a large percentage of world flags.

136
00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.570
But what about Luxembourg?

137
00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:33.400
They claim that they did not actually steal the Dutch flag, even though they are almost identical, but used the colors of the principality of Luxembourg, which, like, okay, fine, sure.

138
00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:42.060
But Luxembourg at some point belonged to the Netherlands, and only afterward did they start using the very flag that looks eerily like the old Dutch flag.

139
00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.650
Never mind, back to the Slavs.

140
00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:47.090
For example, the Croats also used these three colors long ago.

141
00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:58.310
The origin of the modern Croatian flag is actually very interesting, because present-day Croatia, while it was in a personal union with Hungary, was divided into Croatia, Slavonia and Dalmatia.

142
00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:03.650
And when you look at their coats of arms, they really did use those colors even before the pan-Slavic movement.

143
00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:10.150
But this flag arises in 1848, after Croatian nationalists proposed uniting those three territories.

144
00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:15.180
Where do the colors come from? Well, when you join these three regions and merge their flags, you get this.

145
00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:19.740
Still, it is also often stated that the design was influenced precisely by the pan-Slavic movement.

146
00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:24.020
After all, a solid part of the Croatian elite did advocate the unification of the Slavs.

147
00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:30.290
Some even say that these colors were used as a sign of protest aimed at the Habsburgs because they remind of the Russian flag.

148
00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:32.960
And we are well acquainted with the relationship of those two empires.

149
00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:36.630
Look, as with Serbia and Russia, it is hard to say what came first.

150
00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.030
Literally the same question as the chicken or the egg.

151
00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:45.370
It is undoubted that the pan-Slavic flag arose precisely because Slavs used red, blue and white to such an extent.

152
00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:51.220
But it is also undoubted that this template influenced Slavic flags after 1848 to be very similar.

153
00:13:51.360 --> 00:14:01.820
The Croats of course added their own emblem, above all the historical checkerboard with 25 red and white fields, which perhaps represents the red and white Croats, but we would be widening the story too much now.

154
00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:08.920
And on the crown of the coat of arms they placed five shields with the coats of arms of five Croatian regions: Croatia, Dubrovnik, Dalmatia, Istria and Slavonia.

155
00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:15.950
However, the flags of Slovenia and Slovakia are literally just the flags of Russia, as if we added some coat of arms purely so that they tell us apart.

156
00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:24.540
And even that is not quite 100% so, because the Slovenes used these colors as early as the time of the Duchy of Carniola, many hundreds of years ago, from where the colors came.

157
00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.190
So once again chicken and egg.

158
00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:33.380
The flag also arose in 1848, precisely during the national revolutions of Europe, but still a few months before the congress in Prague.

159
00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:39.320
Later they also added this coat of arms, i.e. a shield, which shows the highest mountain in Slovenia, Triglav.

160
00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:46.740
These two lines represent the Adriatic Sea and local rivers, and the three stars represent the coat of arms of the medieval dynasty of Celje.

161
00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:49.230
The Slovak tricolor arose, guess when?

162
00:14:49.230 --> 00:15:01.140
Actually, during the Slovak national awakening and uprising, in the same 1848, they used several versions of this flag, one of which was this color combination, thereby proving that besides Kosovo, Slovakia too is the heart of Serbia.

163
00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:06.160
In the end this combination settled, which at that moment did not create much confusion.

164
00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:11.300
Given that Slovakia was still under Austria-Hungary, they nevertheless also had their own coat of arms.

165
00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:17.060
A double white cross on a red shield, of course, and there are several interpretations of what this actually represents.

166
00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:21.110
Does the first cross represent the death of Jesus Christ and the second his resurrection?

167
00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:25.260
Or Cyril and Methodius, who in the 9th century brought Christianity to this region?

168
00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:29.310
Who knows, but there is a chance that this was the flag of the then principality of Nitra.

169
00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:31.930
Look, damn it, that is the problem with old emblems.

170
00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:37.940
You have multiple theories and interpretations, and nobody can claim with 100% certainty whether any one of them is even correct.

171
00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:42.430
At the bottom of the cross you have three blue Slovak mountain ranges, Tatra, Fatra and Matra.

172
00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:43.660
Cute that it rhymes.

173
00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:47.060
To the sharpest eye this coat of arms will actually seem very familiar.

174
00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:53.740
And that is because it represents half of the coat of arms of a state that is not Slavic at all, but is the creator of this banger.

175
00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.400
What do Hungarians have to do with Slovakia?

176
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:12.620
Slovakia spent most of the last millennium under the control of Budapest, where Hungarians considered Tatra, Fatra and Matra part of their state.

177
00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:19.900
Now, as for the question of why one country still keeps the emblem of another country, that is already a complicated story for which we have no time in this video.

178
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:29.610
But another complicated, interesting story is that this flag was actually originally the flag of Czechoslovakia, while this flag was actually used by Czechia, or more precisely Bohemia.

179
00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:35.160
And then when Czechia and Slovakia freed themselves from Austria-Hungary and united, they had to come up with something new.

180
00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:39.640
And that is why a blue triangle representing Slovakia was added to the Czechoslovak flag.

181
00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:44.340
After the breakup of this state, it was forbidden for either of them to use Czechoslovak emblems.

182
00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:50.260
But Prague in the end just kept this flag, and Slovakia went its own way and nobody was bothered by it.

183
00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:54.720
However, we forgot one Slavic state that almost uses these colors.

184
00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:55.210
Bulgaria.

185
00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:58.640
The Bulgarian flag departs from the standard pan-Slavic template.

186
00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:12.680
One of the reasons why this color is green and not blue is that during their struggle for independence they used this order of colors, and so as to make a difference between them and the Russians, they put in green, because it supposedly represents the fertility of the Bulgarian land.

187
00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:15.370
And with this we have covered quite a few Slavic peoples.

188
00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:24.190
The same way of thinking in designing flags can be found in the Arab world, where all these states use red, white, black and almost always green.

189
00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.900
Where does that come from? Exactly the same reasons as in Africa, America and Europe.

190
00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:33.060
These states also fought for freedom from colonizers, but of course also from the Ottoman Empire.

191
00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:44.110
During the Arab revolt against the Turks in 1916 this flag was created to inspire peoples to overthrow the occupier by joint forces, only for the British and French to come afterward and take everything from them.

192
00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:54.220
And what is the saddest of all, there is a very high likelihood that the design was proposed by the Briton Mark Sykes, who later took part in dividing these territories between London and Paris.

193
00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:57.460
I do not know if you understand the weight of what I just said.

194
00:17:57.460 --> 00:18:04.650
The French and the British incited the Arabs to overthrow the Turks so that afterward they could walk in without any prior obstacles.

195
00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.680
They even supposedly invented a flag for it.

196
00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:09.240
In any case, these colors did not come from nowhere.

197
00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:15.120
The horizontal colors represent three gigantic Arab caliphates: the Abbasid, Umayyad and Rashidun.

198
00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:18.480
Green is also the color of Islam, so there is a broad meaning there.

199
00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:25.620
While red is the color of the Hashemite dynasty, leaders of the revolt, and many states base their flags precisely on those colors.

200
00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:35.580
Jordan, Kuwait, Palestine, the Emirates, Libya and technically also the unrecognized territories Western Sahara and Somaliland, and another short-lived attempt at a union of Iraq and Jordan.

201
00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:41.410
And then there is another version of pan-Arab colors that arose during the 50s: red-white-black.

202
00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:48.920
And what is interesting is that it too arises during national revolts of Arab states, but this time against the French and the British.

203
00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:54.400
Egyptians were the first to apply it, in 1953, and that then influenced the design of today's flag of Egypt.

204
00:18:54.400 --> 00:19:03.540
Then Iraq, Sudan, Syria and Yemen, as well as two more attempts at united Arab states, this time between Egypt and Syria, and then Egypt, Syria and Libya.

205
00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:09.830
And what is especially interesting is that Iraq and Syria originally used that original color combination.

206
00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:16.760
Later, of course, all these states added some emblems of their own, and often precisely of green color in order to differentiate them.

207
00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:25.420
And now in Europe someone else uses a template to mark a shared history: the Nordic countries, specifically Denmark, Sweden, Norway, Finland and Iceland.

208
00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:29.330
All these states use the Nordic cross, but they stole that trick from the Danes.

209
00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:35.300
It may be hard for you to believe now, but at one point Denmark was one of the stronger European powers.

210
00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:40.330
The Danish flag is very likely the longest-used flag in the world, over 800 years.

211
00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:46.060
And no wonder its design influenced the creation of the Swedish, Norwegian, Icelandic and Finnish flags.

212
00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:50.080
Especially after they used this flag in the shared Kalmar Union.

213
00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:55.980
The cross logically represents Christianity, I mean, that should be clear to you, while the red color is of course a symbol of battles.

214
00:19:55.980 --> 00:20:06.440
Except that Norway added a third color to its flag, blue, which symbolizes freedom, and these colors are also a combination of the Danish and Swedish flags, which at some point ruled that country.

215
00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:13.870
Iceland is just an inverted Norway, where blue represents the sea and mountains, white snow, and red the fire of Icelandic volcanoes.

216
00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:18.610
While in Finland blue represents the thousands of Finnish lakes, and white, logically, snow.

217
00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:23.290
In Sweden blue represents justice, loyalty, truth, and yellow generosity.

218
00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:28.520
By the way, this flag template is also used by various regions from Great Britain all the way to Brazil.

219
00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.240
Now then, we mentioned that Chad also revived pan-African colors.

220
00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:36.550
However, when you see this flag, you logically think of... that is right, Andorra.

221
00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:37.830
Just kidding, Romania.

222
00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:47.040
And here is a sentence that I am sure you have never heard in your life: the Chadians pressed the Romanians to change their flag because they supposedly started using it first.

223
00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:49.260
Although Bucharest has used it since the 19th century.

224
00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.540
In fact much longer.

225
00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.880
The Romanian people were divided into three states: Wallachia, Transylvania and Moldavia.

226
00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:57.400
And they had long used combinations of these colors.

227
00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:02.860
And when they united, it all merged nicely into this kind of flag, which had all the familiar colors on it.

228
00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:07.970
And then when they became communists in forty-seven, they slapped on this typical communist coat of arms.

229
00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:13.370
And the Chadians were like: well then we can use those same colors and there will be no confusion.

230
00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:23.030
Technically, they did not steal it from the Romanians either, but wanted to combine pan-African colors with the colors of France, their colonizer, which definitely gives me Stockholm syndrome vibes.

231
00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:27.410
The blue color represents the sky and hope, yellow the desert and sun, and red, you already know.

232
00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:30.780
And okay, they are different enough, at that moment there is no problem.

233
00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:40.880
However, when the Romanians overthrew the man who insulted the people he forced to listen to his speeches, Bucharest again becomes a free state and removes this coat of arms.

234
00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:42.220
And that is where the problem arises.

235
00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:48.360
These flags are now eerily similar, but technically nobody stole anything from anyone, except from the French.

236
00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:56.200
Look, the Romanians placed the stripes vertically and these two colors represented the same thing as these two on the French flag, freedom and brotherhood.

237
00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:59.240
And again after the famous liberté, égalité, fraternité.

238
00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:03.050
Though, in Bucharest's defense, they really had used those colors for a long time.

239
00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:08.680
It is just disputable that they are vertical and in the same order, except for the yellow color, which represents justice.

240
00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:11.020
Still, these two flags are not completely identical.

241
00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:12.900
Chad's colors are subtly darker.

242
00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:20.330
So, if you really look closely, now that you know this difference, you will be able to tell them apart without a problem every time you run into them on the street.

243
00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:24.200
For Moldova the flag is clear, given that they are closely tied to Romania.

244
00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:29.180
They just put a modern version of their old coat of arms with the bovine, which they used for centuries back.

245
00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:32.380
But we are forgetting another victim of French design, Andorra.

246
00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:42.110
That small mountain principality did not have a flag until 1806, when Napoleon handed it this version without the blue color, and then Napoleon the Third added the blue color.

247
00:22:42.110 --> 00:22:46.970
Because the flag was too similar to the Spanish one and they were afraid they would get too close.

248
00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:53.330
Still, the Andorrans, let us say, then rotated the flag by 90 degrees because they got closer to the Spaniards.

249
00:22:53.330 --> 00:23:01.140
And then, when Spain became a fascist country, they rotated the flag back by 90 degrees and added the coat of arms to avoid negative PR.

250
00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:08.610
Andorra does not really have a national identity of its own because there the people are closely tied to both France and Catalonia in Spain.

251
00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:12.990
Andorra even has not one but two princes, neither of whom is from Andorra.

252
00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:17.200
One prince is the president of France, and the other the bishop of Urgell in Spain.

253
00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:20.980
So this flag is precisely a reflection of that, a mix of two cultures.

254
00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:27.670
And since we are on Andorra, right next to it you have Monaco, whose flag is almost the same as the Indonesian one, but they are actually not related at all.

255
00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:29.570
The colors are just tied to local history.

256
00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:33.770
Singapore was to some extent inspired by the Indonesian flag, but also by the Malaysian and Chinese one.

257
00:23:33.770 --> 00:23:37.860
That is why for the Muslim population they have a crescent, and for the Chinese population they have stars.

258
00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:40.160
While the Polish flag has nothing to do with them.

259
00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:44.300
The Syrian and Iraqi flags happen to look alike, just remember that on the Syrian one the green is on the left.

260
00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:46.400
And I think that with this we have actually covered everything.
